      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 30 mg daily is three times the usual maximum dose of 10 mg once daily. Doses that high raise the risk of severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Overdose can also cause prolonged vasodilatory shock. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nWas this a typo? Here are some options:\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily** is the maximum standard dose. Most patients start at 2.5\u20135 mg.\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, titrated up as needed.\n- **Another agent added to amlodipine**, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide, if blood pressure control is the goal and a single drug isn't enough.\n\nIf you really do want 30 mg, tell me and include the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note on the order. Pharmacy will probably want to verify it."
      }
     ],
